A||||10||Fformula88||Looked at an 84 SE today... questions...||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||01-18-2001||10:16 PM||||This evening my father and I went to check out an 84 SE.  I cracked up his 87 Coupe last weekend and due to the excessive rust and corrosion on it, he has decided to look into getting a new Fiero instead of repairing it.  Now for the 84...<P>It has a ground effects package on it.  This package looks like one of the early Fiero race cars.  It comes with an aero spoiler, rocker panel extensions and a fake center scoupe on the trunk that goes over the roof (and it looks GOOD).  The seller claims this was an option on the car new, and was put on by an outside company (from GM) when ordered on the car new at the dealer.  Is this true?  He also says its 1 of 4 made like this.  Is this possible??  I have seen at least one scoupe like this at the FOCOA event in Columbus, and have also seen a couple cars with the ground fx on them. <P>Also, the car has 31K miles on it.  From everywhere I can see it looks the part.  All except the trunk which is very seriously rotted out.  It has HUGE holes on the sides!  The seller is the brother of the original owner and knows a lot of its history.  It had no battery so I didn't see it run, but he is going to get a battery so we can drive it Saturday.  <P>The downside is he is asking way more for an 84 than I think they are worth.  He wants $5000 and claims to be fairly firm.  I know we can get a very good condition late model GT in that price range.  But, if this GFX is really a rare thing, might it be worth a lot more than a standard Fiero?  Right now we are leaning towards a GT but lemme know if this one is worth reconsidering.  Thanx!<P>------------------<BR>John<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">    <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||01-18-2001||10:19 PM||||If you could post a picture of it I might be able to help you out.<P>I know there were some dealer installed body kits, etc. that are unusual and "rare"......GM did not do anything like that, so it is likely a dealer thing.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||87MaroonGTKCMO||01-18-2001||10:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>It has a ground effects package on it.  This package looks like one of the early Fiero race cars.  It comes with an aero spoiler, rocker panel extensions and a fake center scoupe on the trunk that goes over the roof (and it looks GOOD).  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>This sounds like an Indy Pace car. Is the car white? What about the interior, Is it red? How about providing the VIN and some RPO codes.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000003||Fformula88||01-18-2001||10:36 PM||||Sorry, I don't have any pics VIN's or RPO codes.  But it isn't an indy pace car.  I am certain of that.  Just an 84 Fiero SE. It has a tan interior with the suede/sheepskin seat option.<P>It looks kind of like this car.  Obviously it has the stock rear quarters and side scoupe and rear bumper.  But the lower ground fx are about the same and it has the rap around wing on the back.  (not anything like the GT/Formula wing).  Plus it has the overhead scoupe.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/motorcity/1930/sff1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||01-18-2001||10:45 PM||||I found another pic that is closer to what it looks like (and also a real car   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> not a toy in a package!  hehe<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.thisisfun.com/fiero_images/mardis.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Fformula88 (edited 01-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfiero||01-18-2001||11:39 PM||||That answers my question.  I was hoping it looked like the toy car.  There was a dealership here in Denver that built 3 or 4 '84 Fieros to look like an IMSA GTU car (like the toy).  They had the wide body and the engines were turbo charged super duty 4 bangers.<P>The picture of the real car looks like a kit by Kamei.  The wrap around spoiler looks like the IMSA style.  <P>I think $5000 may be a bit much to pay for that car.......is the engine stock or ???||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||01-19-2001||12:07 AM||||If it is a Kamai kit, (which it sounds like) then those really ae fairly rare. That pic of the white car doesn't really look like a Kamai, but I have seen a Fiero with the kit on it and it does look viciously mean.  I think it would be easy to send $5000 to replicate that look. As far as there only being 4 of them, well, yeah, I have a Factory prototype 86 GT to sell ya...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||DJRice||01-19-2001||09:22 AM||||Stimpy, What a coincidence.  I have the factory prototype '87!<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||01-19-2001||09:39 AM||||There may have been 4 made at that dealership. I know that a dealership by me in 1984 and 1985 installed the Kamei kit on a few coupes and called them "SS" Fiero's.<BR>The had the kits and lots of pinstripes on them. The 85's were V-6 SE's. An 84 with the kit isn't worth $5000. If the trunk is that badly rotted that means it sat outside for long periods (not being driven). Are you sure the 31K is correct? If it is 31K and the trunk rotted (means other areas have rust too) I'd say the car is worth no more than $2000 at the most. I personally wouldn't pay more than $1200 just because it sounds a little suspicious with 31K and major rust.||||reg||1
Z||000009||87GT||01-19-2001||10:37 AM||||For 5K, you could buy a really killer Fiero GT, or a superb Formula.  The trunk being rotted out would make me turn around and leave.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Fformula88||01-19-2001||03:25 PM||||To clarify the rust... yeah the trunk is as bad if not worse than it sounds.  Its REALLY rotted, and that worries me.  On the other habd I looked over the underside fairly well.  Aside from a couple spots of rust here and there, its almost perfect.  Mostly surface rust.<P>Orief, I am as sure as I can be that the milage is correct.  I too am incredably suspicious of the low number.  Thats not many miles in 16 years of existance.  But the motor looks good on the outside.  The interior is absolutely mint.  No signs of wear on the seats or carpeting.  If its not the correct milage, there must have been a lot of interior work done to the car.  Also, there is none of the warping of the center console or such areas.  <P>The motor was replaced by the dealer under recall early in its life.  He has the documentation.  So its not original, but the new one was a brand new engine from GM, so it should be fine.<P>I totally agree that the car probably isn't worth 5K.  But it has some awesome two-piece aftermarket wheels (16 inch.) that I would estimate at 1K, plus the body kit and it is loaded.  I think to replicate the car I could easily spend that kind of money for the car, the kit and wheels/tires.  This weekend I am also planning on looking at two GT's (if the snow holds off).  An 87 with about 35K miles for $6200 and one with 52K miles at $5995.  <P>Thanks for all your help!!||||reg||1
